    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 9",
    "text": "-2- ASSISTANCE PROGRAM General The Assistance Program for the College of Forestry of the University of the Philippines was initiated in 1957 under a contract between Cornell University, the University of the Philippines, and what was then the International Coopera- tion Administration of the Uniten States. At that time Cornell University held a similar contract to provide assistance for the College of Agriculture of the University of the Philippines, and it was deemed desirable that Cornell be responsible for both, rather than to involve another United States educational institution. The Corrrell Contract for the College of Forestry extended from April, 1957, to June, 196o. With its termination , responsibility for the pro- gram was shifted to tlie College of Forestry at Syracuse under a new Contract which remained in force until June 20, 1966. Although there were two contractors, each concerned with a particular period of time, the programs were consistent in objective, methods and standar~s. All of the Visiting Professors, except one , were assigned from the College of Forestry at Syracuse, and returned to regular duty after completing their com- mitment to the Contract. (See Table I for listing of Visiting Professors.) Background Situation The College of Forestry of the University of the Philippines was established in 1910 to train men as forest rangers to work on government owned forest land. In 1921 the school was authorized to offer a degree program, but it was staffed and controlled by the Bureau of Forestry. The College· and the Bureau were separated in 1957. The Japanese invasion of the Philippines during the second World War seriously damaged the College buildings, destroyed the library; and scattered the • ... I ·~ - - , . _ t ..., .... ~ J.• • • ' ~. ~ - • ::....00: • -- ,. - ... _,., ~ ...-! -",
