    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 42",
    "text": "-.3 6- Objective 5. Developing effective pro grams of graduate education . research ru1d public information Research had to be largely postponed because of the heavY teaching load that had to be borne by t he resident faculty. Consequently, ther e was only minor incr ease in interest in r esearch by teaching faculty members throughout the project period. Most of the re search initiated under t he Cornell contract was continued , and some new pro jects i ntr oduced . Investigations included six in silviculture, two in forest products , s tudies of the e.conomics of t he wood- using industries of the Philippines, the collection of vital i nformation on the fo r est resources of the Philippines, economic studies on i nternational trade , preparation of guidelines for forest survey using aerial phot os, the est ablishment of continuous inventory pl ots on the Makiling Forest and the development of a management plan for this area. Two other sponsored research projects were undertaken; one on the kaingin problem in Mindanao, and one on t he product.ion of Albizzia falcata for matchwood. The College and Contract staffs devoted considerable effort toward ob- taining a campus and research forest for the College. Success was achieved with the transfer of administration of the Makiling National Park to the Uni- versity of the Philippines by Presidential Proclamation in the fall of 1960. This action was later confirmed with the passage of Republic Act .3523. This Act disestablished the Makiling National Park and transferred the area to the University of the Philippines as a research and demonstration forest for the College of Forestry. It also mandated the establishment of a central forest experiment station by the College. The Act provided for collection of 10 centavos on every cubic meter of wood removed from public forests to provide funds, not only for research, but also for the development of the Makiling Forest, establishment of · a botanic garden, and for forestry extension work. The first monies out of this fund were collected for use in the 1964-65 fiscal year and amounted to some 257, 000 pesos. These funds, however, were",
