    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 49",
    "text": "Physically, the College i s about as well-equipped as the average college of forestry in the United States , although in some areas it is far from the standard of the top- rankin g institutions . It should be mentioned , however , that the C~llege does have access t o certain equipment at the College of Agriculture , f the Forest Pr oduct s Research Institute and even the International Rice Research ' Institute , that can augment what i s available in its own laboratories. The administrative staff of the College of Forest ry in 1957 consist ed of a Dean, a Secretary who was also an instruct or, and a faculty member who served as collecting and disbursing officer. The Dean attempted to carry all adminis- tration himself. As the faculty grew in s i ze and College act ivit ies expanded, the burden on t he Dean became progressively more onerous. It was virt ually impossible for him ·to do all of the staff work necessary for sound decision- making without postponing many important de cisions that needed to be made. The visiting professors worked with the Dean in seeking to share part of the load and to devi se an organizational system to divide functions and responsibilities for better overall administration. To t his end, a formal organizational structure of departments and. adminis- t r ative units was prepared by a faculty administrative organization committ ee wit h the help of the visiting staff and was adopted by the faculty in December, 1962, for a two-year trial period. Other than the office of the Dean, four departments were established -Forest Resources Management, Forest Utilization Engineering, Arts and Sciences, and Forestry Extension, and four administrative units--Office of the Secretary, Office of Business Affairs, Library and Makiling Forest. The connnittee defined the functions of each department and unit and . outlined the responsibilities of each administrative offices. In the case of the departments, the .original acting department chairmen were elected by the ' depart-",
