    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 105, part 1",
    "text": "6 A DEVELOPMENT PROGRAM FOR THE COLLEGE OF AGRICULTURE, UNIVERSITY OF THE PHILIPPINES Introduction This presents a proposed plan for the further development of the U.P. College of Agriculture that should greatly enhance its services to agri- culture and related industries in the Philippines and Southeast Asia. The proposals presented herein aim to strengthen teaching, research, and extension and to increase their effectiveness for the development of agricultural potentials through the region. The general purpose of the study on which the proposals are based was to assist Dean Umali and his staff to draw up a plan that is both desirable and feasible for the development of the College in all of its disciplines. Specifically, the objectives were: 1. To evaluate the adequacy of the College staff, both academic and non-academic, to provide high quality instruction, research, and extension in agriculture for the Philippines and other Southeast Asian countries. 2. To evaluate the curriculum, quality of instruction and research, and adequacy of financial support for all functions of the College. ). To make a study of the physical facilities and services and to suggest appropriate improvements and adjustments that will permit the College to serve more effectively as a distinguished educational institution. This review resulted from a request by Dean D. L . Umali of the U.P . College of Agriculture to the Ford and Rockefeller Foundations, and to other public and private organizations, for financial assistance to underWrite the improvement of the educational, research and extension programs of the Col- lege and its physical facilities . The College staff prepared an excellent \"Proposed Development Program for the U.P. College of Agriculture\" which was discussed with representatives of the Ford and Rockefeller Foundations in February, 1962. Simultaneous with this and in response to earlier communications between Dean Uma.li and Dean C. E . Palm, College of Agriculture , Cornell University, a proposal was prepared in January, 1962, by staff members at Cornell Uni- versity, entitled \"A Program for the Further Development of a Regional Agri - cultural Research and Educational",
