    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 107, part 1",
    "text": "8 the P,hilippines and ~other · countries and will continue to con~ribute toward the overall develoPment .o.f the College as a st+ong educational and re- .search resource . .The most recent favorable feature .in strengthening the College as a ·regibnal research ·center is the establishment by the Ford and Rockefeller .Foundations of· ·tne International Rice Research Institute (IRRI) which is ·operated in ·cooperat-ion ·with the College of Agriculture . This institute will bring together ·outstanding scientists from the important ·rice growing countries of the world to conduct research on all aspects of rice culture. Trainees from many countries are coming to the Ins~~tute for ·research and study and many of them ~ill enroll in graduate :studies at the U.P. College :of Agriculture . Plans have been developed for the location of a Dairy Research and Training Institute at the College under a U.N. Special Fund Project. This should be in operation reasonably soon. All of these agencies and institutes will help in the further develop- ment of the faculty and facilities in order to make it more attractive as an educational and research center for training people for leadership in the Philippines and other nearby countries . There are many advantages in having such a center where students from other countries can study under environ- mental conditions similar to their own. In addition to having made great contributions toward increased food production for the Philippines, the College has advanced markedly in the development of its faculty and facilities for higher quality education and research. Progress is being made in extension education. Its graduates are helping to fill the needs for trained people in all disciplines to give leadership in the rapidly developing agricultural economy. The College must continue to grow, however, if it is to meet its obli- gations now and in the future in educating leaders in agricultural sciences. It must build on present strengths, correct major weaknesses, continue to upgrade its faculty and physical resources, and always strive for standards of excellence in instruction, research, and extension so that it truly can perform its",
