    "text": "sses, continue to upgrade its faculty and physical resources, and always strive for standards of excellence in instruction, research, and extension so that it truly can perform its function as the leading College of Agriculture in the region. Methods and Procedures Used The focal point for starting this review was the \"Proposed Development Program for the U.P. College of Agriculture\" prepared by Dean UmaJ.i and his staff. Careful study was made of this proposal which gives a comprehensive analysis of the present staff and facilities for the functions of the Col- .lege. Justification is given for further development of the staff and the ·research, instruction, and extension ·programs. Special emphasis is given to needs for strengthening graduate studies. In preparation for the review team, Dean UmaJ.i had established four 'faculty committees whose functions were to develop additional summaries- of the needs of the College in the areas of: (a) extension, (b) research, (c) instruction, ~d (d) business ~fai~s.",
