    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 108, part 1",
    "text": "9 I mmediately upon arrival, the consultants were invited to meet with t he Directors' Council to review the plans of procedure. A proposed itinerary was discussed and agreed upon. Much of the first week was spent reviewing the work in the individual department s, as well as in the business office, infirmary, service division, farm operations, office of student affairs, and physical education. Visits were also made to the cooperating tinits, i.e., PACD, ACCI, and IRRI. I n these departmental reviews an analysis was made of course offerings and enrollments, teaching materials used, classrooms and teaching labora- tories, facilities, space and equipment for research, and of research in progress. I n addition, there was an opportunity to talk with a random sample of four to f ive staff members in each department to obtain their judgment on basic needs of the College of Agriculture and of their departments. Through the use of questionnaires much additional information was obtained on pres- ent staff and their formal education, needs for additional staff, limitations in programs, basic needs for equipment, supplies, and physical facilities. Faculty members in charge of the student dormitories and staff housing gave the consultants a good opportunity to observe the present on-campus and off~campus housing for students. Also, needs for staff housing were thoroughly appraised, Considerable time was spent with the College committees on Extension (including the Farm and Home Development program and the Office of Exten- sion and Publications), Research, Instruction (including graduate studies), and Business Affairs. Also, a useful session was held with a special Com- mittee on Academic Appointments and Promotions for the Los Banos Units. One day was spent reviewing the new facilities of the International Rice Research Institute, followed later by a conference with the staff to discuss their training programs and to explore possibilities for any assist- ance they are prepared to give in graduate instruction at the College. Two conferences were held in Manila with Mr. Ingersoll, new country Director for the Agency for International Development (AID), to get acquainted with",
