    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 109, part 2",
    "text": "he faculty and the administration - problems to which solutions must be found. But these problems are being recognized . Furthermore, there appears to be a feeling of confidence on the part of the faculty that the administration is earnestly seeking solutions to the problems. One gets the impression that there are genuine attempts to obtain faculty opinion and participation on matters of policy ~~d procedures and that, to a marked degree, the faculty's right to such participation is being recognized . The recent administrative change whereby the Los Banos units of the University were made the responsibility of a Vice -President for Agricultural Affairs under the President of the University should be conducive to greater efficiency of operation. Within the framework of overall University policy, the new Vice-President should be able to expedite the functioning of the Colleges of Agriculture and Forestry . Furthermore, this arrangement should relieve the President of the U.P. of many administrative chores of a minor nature concerning these two colleges . The consultants are in agreement with the administrative organization which gives responsibilities for given segments of the College program to",
