    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 111, part 1",
    "text": "12 Discussions between the team and representatives of various Committees called at tent ion to the inconvenient location of many of the buildings and other campus facilities. This has resulted from a piecemeal approach to campus planning forced upon the administration by circumstances in the past. The consultants are in agreement with the suggestion that before any furthe+ expansi on ' of facilities is made, a complete campus plan be developed to pro- viqe more efficient and effective use of available space for student and st aff activities. The presence on the College campus of the facilities of cooperating agencies such as ACCI, PACD and IRRI illustrates the wholesome att-itude of the College aaministration toward cooperation with appropriate national and international agencies. Each of these facilities offers the College spe~fic opportunities for service and influence in agricultural education and re- search. Insofar as their objectives and those of the College coincide, the presence of these facilities on campus offers many advantages. The review team shares the concern of the administration, however, that continued expansion on the campus of units having partial or complete auton- omy might eventually endanger the College's ability to meet its primary ob- jectives of providing quality teaching and research. The decision to inte- grate the administration of the proposed Dairy Research Institute with that of the College appears to be a step in the right direction. Size of Staff and Its Quf3-lity The quality of the academic staff is the foundation of any educational institution. Buildings, shiny equipment, library facilities, and motor vehicles, all so essential to a successful teaching unit, hecome nothing more . than curiosities in the hands of inadequately trained instructors and pro- fessors. Competent, productive scientists and educators, on 'the other hand, can make use of these physical facilities in shaping and training the minds of the young people with ,whom they come in contact. For this reason, the visiting team is emphatic in placing competency of staff as the first requi- site of a successful program at Los Banos. During the past 10 years the",
