    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 124, part 1",
    "text": "25 not seem to be on the basis of specific projects . This presents same prob- lems in the administration of departmental research programs and permits excuses for lack of accomplishment on the part of individual researchers. The quality and quantity of research being performed by same of the researchers appear to be especially good. In other cases, however, there is same evidence that research output is low and that th-e quality of re- search needs to be improved. A contimrlng review of research under way at the College by the Research Director might stimulate greater accomplish- ments and upgrade the quality of the research. The College's research laboratories are reasonably well-equipped to carry on applied research and in same cases specialized equipment is avail- able for more basic research . All too often, however, these specialized instruments have succumbed to the rigors of the tropical climate and have be cane inoperative and are in need of repair . The problem of equipment maintenance and repair mentioned in an earlier section is especially acute for the research laboratories . Unfortunately, specific allocations for equipment replacement are missing from the research budgets . Certain specific proposals were made by the research camni ttee for new and/or expanded research facilities and projects. These include the follow- ing: 1. A corn breeding center for Southeast Asia 2. A hortorium and an :Unproved herbarium 3. A food science and technology laboratory 4. A virus and serology laboratory 5. A crop research laboratory 6. A pilot grain storage and processing laboratory 7· An irrigation and drainage research project 8 . An arrlmal disease and parasite control laboratory 9 . A nema,tology laboratory 10. A livestock and poultry introduction and improvement project ll. Miscellaneous facilities to improve research in several projects 12. Liquid funds for research The review team agrees that each of these proposals is worthy of con- sideration and that they would provide opportunities for a greatly expanded research effort. Sane modifications in details and priori ties may be in order and additional projects should be added if the proposed expansion in",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
