    "text": "27 of th Fann and Hane Development program. The review team was pleased with instanc s of good coordination, such as was obtained in Albay Province with th personnel of the PACD, but was skeptica.l of FHD's making its ma.ximum contribution unless such coordination can be worked out elsewhere. Facilities for an expanded extension program are generally l a cking. Office space and conference roams for the new centra.l extension personnel will be needed as will vehicles for field programs. The spa ce and facili- ties for the present infor.mation unit are considerably better than has been the case 1n the past, but are inadequate for a greatly expanded program. At the present time there are no funds available from the University specifically for agricultural extension. In ef fect, extension stands t oday in terms of budget, in the same position as was occupi ed by r esearch 10 years ago . It is being carried on by t he College but t here is no r ecog- nition of this fact in the support the College receives. Such recognition is important if the extension program is to receive per.manent long ter.m support from the Philippine Government. Business and Administrative Affairs The consultants were f avor abl y impressed with the obvious attenti on which has been gi.ven to organizing t he Office of Busi ness Affairs . As the College has grown over the years, administrati ve practi ces, procedures , and responsibilities likewise have devel oped and i ncreased greatly i n thei r significance. According to the Organi zati onal Ma.nu.aJ. of the College, \"the Offi ce of t he Director of Business Aff airs shall be responsi ble primari ly for attend- i ng to t he business transa ctions of t he College . For purposes of assi gning responsi bility, any matter whi ch in t he opi nion of the Dean does not cl earl y fall under ext ension, instruct i on, or research shall be deemed to bel ong t o t he Office of the Di rect or of Busi ness Affairs . \" The maj or units under t he Office of Busi ness Affai rs are the following : a Accounti ng b Collect i ng and disbursi ng c Property d Personnel e Records f Security (g Servi ce The positi on for the Director of Business and Administrative",
