    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 127, part 1",
    "text": "Efforts have been made to speed up the procurement of supplies, mate- rials and equipment but delays in this respect continue to be an important aggravating factor to many staff members. Delays often result in consid- erable inefficiencies of operation. Possibilities for the establishment of a procurement office in Manila are being explored in an effort to re- lieve academic staff members of the use of their valuable time in checking on the status of specific requisitions. Also, the semi-autonany provided for the Los Banos units of the U. P. may improve procurement efficiency for small requisitions. A most desirable policy of revolving budgets has been established in sane units of the College, such as Animal Husbandry. This policy provides necessary and desirable flexibility in the use of funds and might well be extended to other departments and units so that receipts from sales could be used for same of the operational expenses. The consultants were impressed by the interest of the College Admin- istration in the welfare of its non-academic personnel and the progress that has been made in upgrading their econanic status. Unfortunately, across the board raises in salary increase the wages of all employees with- out regard to canpetency. There is need for a system that will make it possible to raise the wage ceiling and give greater encouragement to the most competent employees who have the greatest potentials. The College is dependent upon the availability of adequate utilities and services for efficient functioning. Among the essential s_ervices are electric power · and water distribution, transportation, telephones, medical care, security, and maintenance and repair of the physical plant and equip- ment. Unfortunately, the budget of the service division is inadequate to finance the performance of the essential functions of the division. There is inadequate space for offices and shops for the electrical section, garage for the motor pool, working space for the carpentry shop, metal shop, or storage space for supplies. With two exceptions, the vehicles of the divi- sion are old and several are badly in need of replacement. A growing problem and health hazard to",
