    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 155, part 1",
    "text": "Estimated Costs of Development Progrrum An attempt has been made to estimate and summarize the costs of a develop- ment program as outlined in this report. Consideration has been given to ~­ recurring expenses for capital construction and facilities and to annually recurring costs for salaries, equipment and supplies, and other operating ex- penses. Non-recurring Costs A summary of the expected costs of new construction and renovation of exist- ing buildings is given in Table 19. New buildings and annexes are estimated to cost about 12.4 million pesos, whereas renovation of present facilities will likely be considerably less expensive, some 1.7 million pesos being the estimated cost. In Table 12 anticipated costs for all the non-recurring capital improve- ment projects are summarized. The total is in excess of 24.5 million pesos. The consultants emphasize that these estimates should be used with caution since they are necessarily based on very general information on building costs in the Philippines. Also, it is extremely difficult to estimate the cost of improved services, such as the sewage system, without first knowing more about building locations, feasibility of separate small sewage disposal units and re- lated factors. The consultants feel strongzy that the capital construction should be of such quality as to permit intensive usage over the years with as little annual maintenance as possible. Fancy architectural \"trirmnings\" should receive low priority in comparison with human comfort and with the utility and length of life of the facilities. For example, it is expected that the \"rental\" houses (see Table 12) would be constructed of concrete and the best pretreated lumber to reduce d.amage from termites and the weather. This type of construction should provide facilities which are adequate at the present time and which would require l mv annual maintenance in the future. Estimates presented in Tables 12 and 19 do not include costs for standard equipment to be used in the facilities. The consultants assumed equipment costs to be about 20 per cent of those tor the capital construction and service proj- ects . Total facility and equipment cost estimates,",
