    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 209",
    "text": "- i - ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS My cordial association with Mr. J. J. Flor bas been most appre- ciated. Dr. F. A. Bernardo was responsible for compiling the space and equipment requests of the departments and preparing the development plan for the Campus. He was most helpful in the working out of the more detailed aspects of the program as the actual planning of the buildings by the architects took place. When he left for the United States in the Fall of 1965, his presence was sorely missed. As the staff core of the five- year development program, these two men have been most effective in keeping the program moving along as rapidly as possible. Mr. Floris an exceptionally well-qualified Project Manager. The College is indeed fortunate to have him in charge. Dr. Gilbert Levine had taken a great interest in the building prog- ram. Before his return to Ithaca, he passed on to the Technical Staff 'the many ideas and suggestions which bad occurred to him. Dean Umali and his administration have exerted every possible effort to provide us with adequate office space where the project work could be effectively con- ducted. Dr. Herbert L. Everett aas aided us in many ways which have contributed to making this activity a pleasant experience. It was a great privilege to be appointed a member of the Dean's Directors' Council and of the Executive Committee. It has thereby been possible for me to keep in touch with campus plans, policies and problems",
