    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 212",
    "text": "THE BUILDING PROGRAM The progress and problems involved in a large and significant development program such as this are documented in considerable detail in the belief that this may prove of interest to some other ins- titutions and countries. Thus, they may be able better to anticipate the difficulties which can be encountered and benefit from an under- standing of some of the ways in which they might be overcome. Several preliminary meetings were held by Dean Umali and the Technical Staff with the architects who had been selected, with World Bank approval, to design the buildings. Their fees, the timetable for plans and construction and the philosophy for the development of the whole Campus were discussed and agreement reached. The contracts for the services of the architects were signed ·by President Romulo and them on November 27, 1964. Mr. A. E. Nakpil was to serve as supervising architect to assure strict adherence to the basic principles and objectives of the Master Plan. In addition, he was to design the Physical Sciences Building. Mr. C. D. Arguelles was to do the Biological Sciences Building, Mr. L. V. Locsin- the Student Union and the Dormitories 1 and Mr. F. M. Mendoza - the Food Science and Agronomy-Soils Buildings. The DCCD Engineering Corporation, represented by Mr. L. Un. Ocampo was responsible for the site utilities. It was also to do the",
