    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 355",
    "text": "II. y 1. ) Th main limiting factor is the lack of an actual r search atmosphere in which graduate students and rofessors discuss their research projects and stimulate each other. Despite the strength of Soils Department research programs relative to other parts of the College 7 the Soils Department's atmosphere is mainly that of a teaching in$titution. b) One of the most $erious limitations is the lack of long range research objectives 7 i.e., what problems should the Soils Department solve in the next five or ten years. Most research projects are now unrelated; some are repetitions of work previously done. c) Lack of a comprehensive knowledge of previous research work done in the Philippines. A tremendous amount of data is being stored in the Department's Annual Research Reports in a very disorganized way. The importance of library work has not been emphasized enough to the graduate students and the staff members carrying out research. d) Lack of knowledge of the particular conditions and literature on tropical soils. Frankly, I was shocked wh n I first attended the graduate soils seminars, b caus r f r nc",
