    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 357",
    "text": "THE PROCESS OF COMMUNTIY DIFFERENTIATION : INSIGHI' l'ID DEVELOPMENT ~ !sao Fujimoto -oOCo- One of the basic assumptions of science is that there is order in na.- ture . We recognize diversity but we also search for unity. Tre literally millions of distinct plants and animals are subsume d by the unifying p:r:inci- ples of evolution. Mendeleev' s periodic tabl e of the elements and quantum theory clarify what it is that is common to all compounds, whether known or yet to be put together . The genet i c l aws of Mendel and t he Law of Gr avity likewise offer order l y expe ctations f rom a morass of observations . Just as alchemy has been removed f rom chemistry, we might ask whether it is now possi- ble t o substitute illumina tion for myst ery in understanding the process of community developmento We spe ak of conmnmitie s and corrmunity developnent but what do we !mow about how communitiB s develop? Are the re any r egularities to the pattern of comnnmity growth - or stagnation? We recognize the diversity of cornmunit:ies, not only among different cultural and national settings , but within the same r egion or within ths same network of an intervillage system. Are we to account for these differences as due to the random evolution of communities , and, hence ~ committed to approach each community as a unique standing of communities and their development? 0() c Pt.J vv e: 1 D c: r-J'T1 Y A rJ 'I P r<...c c, ~ TH T ~, '- C'' I l'J',( r r Y<:1HnA11C. L.(IJO( ~2S1A\" 1 DINC'; Of (oMIV\\l.\\NI11E.S A't..JoTHE.tR. E \"·L It is the intent of this paper t o suggest that the answer to tm last quest i on is ~ · The answer will be given from the framework of cybernetics information theory, and the application of Guttman scale analysis . What .** P a.-oer presented at too Fourth Annual Philippine Sociological ociety meetings : May 25-28 1 1965 . Mindanao State University, Mar awi City IIW~'~ del Sur. '",
