    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 418",
    "text": "PROGRAM GOALS AND PROGRESS The recognized mother of invention is neces sity. The father is a bit more difficult to identify. Perhaps ingenuity is a rea sonable choice. In any event, University Administrators mus t use the offspring of t his mating repeatedly to achieve the diverse supports needed for p rogramming instruction, research, and extension. D emands on the U. P . College of Agriculture are ever changing and seemingly ever expanding. The UP-Cornell Graduate Education P rogram seeks to give imaginative support to one of the p rominent p res sing areas of College cor.amitment. \\/The need and desire for an atmosphere of increasing academic excellence is recognized by Univer s ities everywhere. The UPCA is no exception. The high calibre of past performance has given rise to present p roblems . This is true because many young staff have completed advanced study abroad, and now der.aand increased opportunity on the local camp us. Such demands are logical and helpful only if the administration can re spond so as to channel restless brain power into productive creative activity.",
