    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 427",
    "text": "- 10 - and communications is the p r ime con s i de r a t ion o£ a visiting consultant. Wor kin g p rogr ams £o r t he Colle g e a a well a a cooperat i v e appr oaches t o t he ?repo sed Mass C ommunicat ion s Cent e r a t Diliman will be developed. T he six g r aduat e s tudent as sis tants from Cornell a re p erhaps at the c enter of the Gr aduate E duca tion P rogram. E xc e r pt s from their prog r ess r eports a nd re~arks from t h eir w ives reveal the broad r ange of a ctivitie s as well a s the contri- butions a n d p roblem s c ha r a cte rizing these student f a milies: \\; If the thesis research has been the meat and p otatoes of my Los Bafios exp erience, then the teach- ing assignments have been the gravy. The opportunity to get acquainted with U P CA undergraduates and to obs erve their classroom performance has been truly rewarding. In both the beginning and the advanced courses, I found the students to respond quite like a normal group of students anywhere. A few individuals were outstanding, easily grasping the material presented and sometimes showing initiative to go beyond. A few individuals failed, usually from lack of application rather than lack of ability. The great bulk of the class, however, fell in the category of average ability, but with a surprising degree of inquisitiveness and interest in the material. Despite remarks which I have heard to the contrary, I found that these students, if treated like mature College students, will respond accordingly. (Animal Husbandry) The main problem is getting one's research \"off the ground.\" This problern is obviously not peculiar to this location, but it can become more acute where one has to develop a technique more or less from scratch while at Los Banos.",
