    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 428",
    "text": "... 1 1 - Another reason for setting an early start on research is the difficulty of purchasing needed supplies . The t ime involved in receiving orders from the United St a t es is now familiar to everyone on t he p roject. However, many it ems are availabl e in Manila but t he search f o r t hem can be a long and ardu ous p r ocess . The purchas i ng of supplies in Manila c an be eas e d by by - pas s ing t he C olleg e p ur c hao - in g s y s tem ; t hat is , by pur c has ing f or c ash and a pplying f or reimbur sement. Obviously t hi s i s not the best long- term p r o cedur e for t he College as a whole. However, t h i s is a grea t t ime- save r as compared with the p re s ent C ollege -purchas ing p roc edur e. In many c a ses it is advantag eous for Cornell visiting s taff to use this m ethod of p urchas ing until the College p urch asing p rocedure can be revamped. (A gronomy) T h ere is no substitute for a ctua lly living in and exp eriencing a culture, but one can do this a nd still not und erstand m uch of w hat one is exp eriencing. For this rea son, I would j ust s uggest a couple of things for o r ientation to this p roject. 1. M a k ing use of the m any readings on the culture s of the P hilippines, especia lly the training materials of the P e a ce Corp s. A t least one could then approach the situation with s ome sensitivity to the new cultural values one will be encountering. 2. P erhap s it would do the p roject well to p ut more emphasis on the study of Taga log - not to necessarily be- com e fluent, for that is difficult in a community where virtually everyone uses English most of the time. But a t lea st to lea rn the amenities, for that symbolic gesture I seem s to be m uch a ppreciated. (graduate wife) P resently, many proj ects and innovations introduced in the b a rrios fail of expectations. Cooperatives fail, clinics remain unused, and local governments exist in name only. The explanation given where such results occur is usually: \"The community wasn't ready for it. 11 '~That is a community ready for, and what preconditions are related to readiness of different stages of differentiation? The",
