    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 429",
    "text": "- 12 - research design will include a study of the success or failure of selected projects and how that is related to the differentia tion level of the community. (Agricultural Education} Both students and s taff members should be encouraged to plan more extensive and more enthusiastic research p rograms which include imaginative new approaches to their res p ective problems. Cooperative research between departments should be encouraged and rewarded; it is done supe rficially at ? resent, but involves no true mutual res pe ct a nd coop eration. (P lant Breeding) I have been completely taken by the generosity of p eop le here . In the barrio where I teach, v:re have become friendly with several wonderfu.1 families, and have visited with them in their hon:e s until our Tagalog and their English gave out. Alt hough they are poor, they are so hospitable, willing and wanting to give us all they have. The children in my classes often drop over to visit, and several children work to earn money for school. {graduate wife) The lecture sections were in general overcrowded with inadequate lighting, blackboard spa ce, and audio facilities. Many students in the last few rows of the lecture hall could neither hear the lecturer nor read the material presented on the blackboard. This resulted in an additional load being added to the crowded schedules of the laboratory instructors, since the students required additional lectures and explanation of the lecture material in addition to a laboratory schedule overcrowded with experiments. {graduate teaching assistant) As the end of the first year in Los Bafios is nearing one realizes that the exchange program we are on is a two - way exchange . Not only is aid and advice being ' given to the College of Agriculture but we are also obtain- ing a greater depth of patience, consideration and under- standing from otlr experiences here . (graduate wife)",
