    "text": "- 14 - Thi s br oad r e l a tio n s hip of visiting f a culty a nd U P CA activity i s r eflected in the following quotations from annual r eports : Because of the U P CA ' s leadership role in the A ssociation of Agricultural Colleges of the Philippines (A CAP) and because the Director of Extension Education came on the scene after ACA 1? had been operating for one year, there was a need to explore the needs and interest of the various member institutions . The Director of Extension Education and the Extension Consultant have visited seven of the Colleges and held conferences with administrative p ersonnel and faculty . As a result o£ these conferences, the Director of Extension Education has p repared a p rop osal for a conference (workshop) on extension work. This proposal is being brought to the attention of the ACA P executive committee. (Extension Area} In p reparation for the course in instrumental analysis , I designed and wrote u p a series of experiments of increas- ing complexity to illustrate the function and use of electrical devices and of simple circuits. Subsequently, these cir- cuits were used for the solution of analytical problems . All parts for a particular experiment were mounted on a ?anel and the students were required to wire t hem, guided by a schematic wagram using conventional symbols whose arrangement was quite different from that on the panel . By using special snap fasteners, wiring could be done very quickly if you knew where wires were needed. These experiments were unconventional in rnost cases. They were designed so that the student could discover new relationships for himself. (Physical Sciences Area} It was a great privilege to be appointed as a member of the Dean's Direct'\"'rs' Council and of the Executive Committee. All meetings of these have been attended. It has thereby been possible to keep in touch with campus plans , problems , policies , and activities. This aided in",
