    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 537",
    "text": "- '72 - .. Fil st, working with a perennial crop such as coconuts always prco nts so1ne difficulties when attempting to measure the production r sponse to price. One of t he most interesting quest ions is the effect that decontrol le gi s l at1on (which since 1960 has given a s erie s of boosts to price) ha s upon production . It takes approxim ately seven year s b efor e a new coconut t r ee comes into production. There are no r e cords available of 1~e w plantings. Mr. Nyberg- is now surveying p roduce rs to obtain what information he can on decis ions regarding new plantings. Anothe r interestL1g question is how the copra buying price is determined by the importing countries . It is frequently cla.L.-n.ed that Ca rgill in the Unite d States and Unilever in Europe have divided up the world market and act as n10:1opsonists in buying copra. It is als0 said that they are r e sponsible for actions to curb coconut oil pro· · duction in the Philippines. Thus far 1 it has been difficult to locate reliable sources in the Philippines who are thoroughly familiar with the pricing procedures of the compat1ies in the rnajor importing coun- tries. It v;ould be desirable for Mr. Nyberg to visit some of these companies on his r eturn trip to the United States to obtain further information on this subject. Research on Fertilizer Response The fertilizer study is entitled, \"Analysis of Fertilizer Res- ponse and Profitability under Risk and Uncertainty,\" and registered",
