    "text": ".. 73 - as Research Project No. 2405 . Funds set aside fo r this pr oject amount t o :?3 880 his s udy was undertaken with the cooperat ion of the following age cies : Department of Soils - UPCA, Bureau of Soils - DANR, the Phi ppine Sugar Institute, UPCO and the International Ric e Resea..rch Instit ute . Two que stions need to be answered: (1) what are t he yield responses to the applicat ion of fertilizer for a given crop under spe- cific condit ions , and (2) how can the yield res ponse be related in a meaningful wrxy t o the probability of achieving a return in excess of fe rtili zer expense A number of agencies, both public and private, have conducted fe rtilizer experiments throughout the Philippines, The major ~rops fo r which fertilizer response work has been conducted are rice, corn, and sugar ~ane. This information has never been gathered together in a central location, Nevertheless, there appears to be sufficient inform~tion availaple in the case. of the crops indicated to answer the above questions, Specific objectives of the study are as follows: 1. Assemble the available fertilizer response data for rice, corn, and sugar cane. 2. Analyze differences in response under differences in major input factors - soil type, water availability, and variety as well as fertilizer level. 3.. For specified situations examine the distribution in.., yields at given ~19 of fertilizer application to determine: (a) the yield that can be expected for a specified probab- ility level and a given level of fertilizer application, or",
