    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 539",
    "text": "- 74- • alternatively, (b) the fertilizer required for a specified yield and probability level. 4. Determine the optimum level of fertilizer application for fertilizer functions representing a specified probability level (e. g. 50o/o, 80o/o). Mr. Antiporta has been primarily responsible for the data ollection. A considerable amount of progress has been made in t his areao and some preliminary analyses have been conducted. Each separate experiment has been recorded on a 5 x 8 McBee card and given a code number. All pertinent data that can be obtained regard- ing the conduct of the experimert is recorded o:n this card. This includes information on crop, variety 1 soil type 1 residual nutrients in soil, fertilizer rate and yield for each replication etc. It is sur- prising how much of this basic information is missing in many of the experimental records. The Bureau of Soils conducts all of its experimental work on rice and corn in farmers ·: fields, principally with seed board approved ... . varieties. Thus_, the results are much closer to the kind of response that would be obtained by farmers in actual practice. Information on over 125 rice experiments conducted throughout the P hilippines from the period 1952-54 to 1964-65 has been collected from this agency. Information on the corn experiments is currently being collected. The United Nations Special Fund has financed a five year projects in \"\",.tilizer experimental work in the Philippines. This group is mental 8 '--~ r1 in the Bureau of Soils and has already conducted a",
