    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 541",
    "text": "... 7 search Activi i s 1) A r. udy was undertaken to investigate the effect of the recent e support program (Republic Act 4643 passed March 8 1 1966) on rice production. The objective of this investigation was to determine the effect on hectarage and rice yield of the twenty per cent incr ease in the price of rice . The quantitative phase of this analysis was based upon the previou s research in r ic~ s upply resp ons e conduct e d by Mahar Mangahas and V e r non Ruttan, e conomis ts at IRRI. The results of this inve stigation we r e r eported at t he IRRI seminar on 1966. The paper will b e publishe d in the Philippine Agricul- The conclus ions of t hi s paper are as follows: \"We can con clude that the pric e s upport program will m aintain the balance in the t e rms of trade between t he e xport and t he food pr<:> ducing s e ctors. The r e is n o reason tc believe that the r e will be a sub stantial shift i n hecta rage b ~ tween r ic e and the competing crops. However, there i s a definite need for r es e=trch t o e xamine rn ore clos ely the nature of hectarage competition . Vve n e ~ m or e inforrnation not only on the wa y in which differ ent land areas respond, but also on the way in w·hich diffe r ent groups of people (for e xample , landlords a11d tenants) respond to price inc entive s. Finally 1 the big quest - ion mark is, what will happen to yields. We cannot answe r this question. However, the r e s e arch analysis undertaken to explain year to year changes in yields in the regions of the Philippines will prove useful. When yields do increase , we will be able to determine whether or not this increase was due s imply to weathe r or to changes in hectarage, or whether it repr esents a r eal breakthrough. \" 2) 'l,he last line s of the above paragraph refer to a second in- formal study now unde rway also b eing conducted with the assistance of Mr. Anti porta. This is an investigation of the factors affecting year to year change s in rice yields in the regions of the Philippines. The",
