    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 809",
    "text": "i FORE NORD AND ACKNOWLEDGE iv;ENT T h e preparation of the a nnual r e port for the fourth year of the U J?CO (U P -Cornell Gradua te Education Program) project has provided the occasion to reapprai se the program. By taking the o pportunity to reflect u p on the w ork it can be determined whether it h as b e en fruitful. To be significant, progress has to be measured a s it r e l a tes to the total p lan of develop1nent of the U. P . College of Agricu lture {UPC A ). To p roceed with this, a li s t of U P CA and U:?CO accomplishments wac p r epared. From the list of 81 accom- pli shments, it will be ob served that it w as a productive year at UPCA. In evaluating the entir e p rogram it is obvious that there is an increas ing demand for education at a higher level. The College today is stronger than it has ever b e en before. Thus it faces more respon- sibilities in its approach to greater opportunities. These are but a challenge to continued growth and development. Today, UPCA has greater challenges to its ingenuity and vision; there is no limit, however, to the imagination that can be injected into the future. The extent to which this is accomplished will determine what U P CA will be like 10 years from now. At the moment. the entire staff can take a justifiable rrleasure of pride in the achievements to date while developing a concern for UPCA' s continued strong position",
