    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 993",
    "text": "- 19 - REPORTS BY VISITING PROFESSORS AND GRADUATE STUDENTS July 1, 1967 - J une 30, 1968 ANIMAL SCIENCES J.c. Miller Visi t i ng Professor in Anima l Husbandry Introduction The writer received a warm welcome by the Animal Husbandry staff on his arrival near the end of July 1967. Thanks to the staff, he has been privileged to travel to most of the larger islands in an effort t o survey the total livestock potential, with emphasis on beef cattle. A maj or share of his time has been devoted to a study of the present and potential beef industry of the Philippines and t o developing r e sea rch proposals for beef cattle management studies. He has had no formal teaching assignments but has participated in departmental seminars and one off-campus short course. For purposes of clarity and brevity this report is divided into six sections, namely: (1) Staff, (2) Instruction, (3) Research, (4) Facilities, (5) Activities of the Visiting Professor, and (6) Summary and Recommendations. Staff Present Status Number Ph.D. Degree Professors 2 (emeritus only) 2 Associate Professors 2 1 Assistant Professors 14 10 Instructors 27 0 Research Associates 3 0 Research Assistants 10 0 Total 58 13",
