    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 999",
    "text": "- 25 - Summary and Recommendations 1. The department has a competent, well-trained staff. 2. Sub~t~tial progress is being made in upgrading the formal tra1n1ng ~f the staff. Three Ph.D. degree holders were added dur1ng the current year and 010 more will be added early in the coming academic year. 3. The level of instruction, both graduate and undergraduate is being improved as the training and experience of the staff is strengthened. 4. There is need for Philippine textbooks and reference material based on and adapted to Philippine conditions. 5. Greater emphasis should be given to management research involving the application of nutrition, physiology and genetics to Philippine environments. 6. Much of the routine care of experimental animals is done by seniors s~d grP.du~te assistants. Closer supervision by project leaders to improve the husbandry will make the results more meaningful. 7. The dairy division is faced with some fundamental decisions. A self analysis, with the establishment~£ long range goals and priorities is paramount. Immediate~ulling and reduction of herd size to fit the budget and improving feed production capacity of the available land should receive top priority. 8. The time has arrived when the UPCA administration needs to decide the future of its cattle program. Cattle are primarily forage-consuming animals. This is especially true in a concen- trate deficit country like tha Philippines. The land currently available to the dairy and beef cattle divisions combined totals about 50 hectares, with approximately half of it subject to irrigation. The year around feed producing capacity of this land is far too low to support the animals necessary to give UPCA a meaningful teaahing and research cattle program. There are three alternatives: 1. Reduce herd size and program to what the budget and land will support. 2. Increase budget to purchase additional feed 3. Acquire additional land at UPCA or establish one or more branch research stations.",
