    "text": "- 15 - Introduction of New Horticultural Products During the past year a few new implements and products of use in horticulture have been introduced and evaluated in the Vegetable Crops Section. Most of these items have been accepted ~y the section for use in their various programs. Also, var1ou~ types of containers for starting seedlings are currently be1ng evaluated in an undergraduate student's thesis. Teaching Agronomy 5 The author i s currently handl i ng a l aboratory section of 20 students in Agronomy 5, Genera l Horticul ture. In the past , much of his t i me in teach i ng has been spent working with Agronomy 5 outs i de the classroom. This has inc l uded assistance given to Mr . Ismael Anunciado in his task of coordinating lecture and l ab, and the preparation of two new laboratory exercises. These labo ra tory exercises deal with home gardening and a plant sale. Seminar During the year this writer has been encouraging the idea of a s eminar i n horticulture and it has developed to the point t hat a seri es of seminars will be offered in the horti~ulture s ec t i on for the current college year. Extension Tra i ning The author has assisted the vegetable crops staff i n planning the training course that has been offered to severa l groups of Peace Corps Volunteer~ and has participated in the ac tual training of two such groups. The author and Miss Cherry Villegas were responsible for planning the lecture and laboratory series offered in the three-month training of two such groups.",
