    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1393",
    "text": "9 the Philippines on September 8, 1970 and returned to Cornell on May 31, 1972. Mr. l~arren R. Philipson arrived in Los Banos on August 6, 1970 and has worked in the Department of Soils. He has developed and taught a course in \"Introduction to Aerial Photographs\" and presented information on aerial photographic analysis in a special topics and research problems course. In addition to these efforts, Mr. Philipson has developed syllabi for two courses entitled 'Aerial Photographs for Land Analysis' and 'Environment and Land Use' which will be a part of the graduate program in environmental studies which the Department of Soils -::) ! -~ intends to develop. He 'tvas instrumental in the reproduction I .. : of the six-volume work 'Land Form Reports' which has been ,,., , .. distributed to several institutions in the Philippines and will greatly aid in aerial photograph interpretation. Mr. Philipson's thesis study entitled 'Airphoto-Crop Analysis ~: • -. I in Tropical Resource Ev~1uation' has involved cooperative efforts with technicians of t~e Bureau of Soils who have assisted in the identification of crqps groW11 on soil units in the various clima~ic zones. Mr. Philipson will lea~e Los Banos on June 25, l972 to complete hi~ thesis at Cotnell. Contribution of UPCO vliv!:~. r, As in the past, the UPCO wives, though fewer in number, have participated in many organizations and events for the betterment of the community. In addition to the organized",
