    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1394",
    "text": "10 women's groups like Suhay , Quebala and Maquiling Ladies, the help of the wives and children in entertaining visiting guests, reading to grade school children and helping t he sick and needy should be recognized. The UPCO library , which had grown to s everal hundred volumes was dis t ributed to t he UPCA library, t he Rural High School library and the br owsing room of the Depart ment of Humanities. Thank you l adies f or all your help . :. and encouragement. .._ .......... : Cornel l Visitors While f ar from the United States, past linkages between Cornell and t he UPCA and the gr~ving number of 'alumni' are reasons for t he popularity of Los Banos as a stop on many Cornellian 's i tinerary of travel in Southeast Asia. During the past year we have had the pleasure of the follm·dng company: Dr. J. F. Metz, former UPCO Project Leader, while he was in the Philippines as consultant to the national task force on research. : . ·. _, Mr. and I1rs. David l~illiams. Dave is advisor to inter- national students at Cornell and visited with the many Cornell alumni both at Los Banos and in the greater Manila area. Dr. Thomas T. Poleman and Mr. Weyland Beeghly spent a sig- nificant amount of time i -- setting up and conducting a cooperative -:jf!C) .... ~-· study with IRRI on the h~ energy required for different operations in rice production. Both Dr. Poleman and Mr. Beeghly are in the Department of Agricultural Economics at Cornell.",
