    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1395",
    "text": ": 11 Drs. Edward H. Glass and H. David Thurston who were previ ous participm1ts in the UPCO project, returned as members of a pest management study team. Prof. and Mrs. Russel D. Martin. Russ is a member of the Department of Communication Arts at Cornell and stopped at Los Banos to visit with people in the communication area. He was on a special assignment for the Director of Extension at Cornell. Dr. and Mrs. Jacob Kampen, former UPCO participants, -' :· .. ;.t \\ . visited en route from India to the U.S. They were hosted by the Senen Mirandas and reviewed progress on the Upper Pampanga River irrigation project in addition to renewing old acquaintances • • 0 ·t; ·i while here • l --!J; . ~ ... ! Mr. Jerry Wilcox visited just before the project terminated. Jerry works in Dave William's office at Cornell and was interview- ing former foreign students at Cornell to determine their impressions on how their period of study could have been improved '· J ;, _i to better prepare them for their occupations in their home countries. UPCA PARTICIPANTS Graduate Assistants in the United States: Four graduate assi~ tants who were working toward their Ph.D. degrees at the beginning of the year have returned to Los Banos during the year, and two more are still in the u.s.",
