    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1398",
    "text": "14 :I; '. 'Some selected factors associated with emphatic abi l i ty of farm management technicians in the Philippines. ' The thesis has been sent to Cornell for final duplication and processing. Mr. Juliano will receive the Ph.D. degree in August 1972, and expects to con- tinue his assignment in the Farm and Home Development Office. Mr. Elpidio L. Rosario successfully defended his thesis entitled 'Physiological aspects of photosynthesis differences in relation to yield exhibited by some sugarcane varieties' .. . 'I. • •• on March 29, 1972. The Ph.D. degree was awarded in June 1972. Dr. Rosario will continue his work on the physiology of sugar cane in the Department of Agronomy. Mr. Percy E. Sajise completed the requirements for the Ph.D. from Cornell with the defense of his thesis entitled 'Evaluation of cogon (Imperata czlindrica (L.) Beauv.) as a seral stage in Philippine vegeta£ional succession. I. The cogonal seral stage and plant succession. II. Autecological studies on cogon.' on March 29, 1972. The degree was awarded in June 1972. Dr. Sajise will continue his work in ecology in the Department of Agricultural Botany. ; .: .J ~· Thesis Research at Los Banos: Three Filipino participants are still conducting their thesis research at UPCA ns part of the requirement for degrees from Cornell. As mentioned earlier in this report, Mr. Senen Miranda returned to Los Banos in 1971 and is conducting an in- vestigation on water management at several locations in the",
