    "text": "DEPART11ENT OF AGRICULTURAL ECONOMICS Salient Facts About the De partment The department staff is composed of 42 academic (28 teaching and 14 non-teaching) and 11 non-a cademic members. The number has doubled for the past decade . Of the academic force, 7 a re Ph . D. degree holdexs; 11 M. S. , and 24 BoSoAo Within the next 5 years , 11 staff members are expected to obtain the Ph .D . and 15, the M. S . degree. Student Enrollment The average annual enrollment from 1958 to 1967 at the Department of Agricultural Economi cs was 1,292 . For the academic year 1966-67, 1,378 enrolled in the different Agricultural Economics courses, an increase of 66 (5%) over that of 1965-66 . From 1911 to 1967, 252 BoS oAo degree holders had Agricultural Economics as their major field of specialization . Since 1955, the depart- ment has graduated 16 MoSo students, including 2 Pakistanis o At present, the department has 105 undergraduate major students and 22 M.. S. Number of Courses Offered The department offers 17 undergraduate and 11 graduate courses . An additional 2 graduate courses are to be offered soon. Research From 1919 to 1967, 370 research studies have been completed . Of these studies, 186 were published as technical papers in The Philippine Agriculturist . The total number of current and planned (for the immediate future) research projects is 105 .",
