    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1815, part 1",
    "text": ",5 - College bound students will be advised after the firs t year to transfer to a college preparatory high school Should the faci- lities of th barrio high school prove adequate , option al subjects for college preparation mqy be given if enough students desire to go to college . 8 Barrio people provide basic salary of t eacher s - - the government and/or other source provide the incentive fund to be added to the basic salar,y of dedicated and effective t eache rs. V. Philosophical Fr ame The philosophy behind this pilot barrio high school is re- fle eted on the following ideas: 1 . Appro aches to rural development may b e viewed as eith er instantaneous or long range, Instantaneous approach usually brings about temporary physical improvement so that when the time dimension is cons:ii.dered the \"ningas cogan\" phenomenon becomes the rule rather than the exception , The long range approach lean is heavily on the process of syste~ atic and functional human resource development (edu9ational process) aimed at lasting and continuing rural improve- ment . These two views correspond to the maxim: 11 If you give a man a fish you feed him for a day, if you teach a man ~ !£. ~ you feed him for a life t:ime . 11 It is the _latter view that the barrio high school is envisioned to play a vj tal role in the Philippine rural and agricultural development) 2. Fundamentally, the barrio prople should aim at the develop- ment of better rural life; better homes; more efficient utilization of resources and higher productivity; and active~ participating citizenry. 3• Principally, these can be attained by means of c:.n educational process dominantly guided by the educational principles of \"learning by doing. 11 Thus , education of barrio poople , to be useful, should be problem-solving centered. Life in the barrio is faced with pro- blems. The students should know how to identify and solve these problems by actually identifying and solving them. By this pro~ess the students develop both manipulative and decision-making skills and abilities which are essential to profitable and successful entre- preneurial ventures. 4. Young people who will devote the ir time in improving their",
