    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 1835",
    "text": "- 12 ... of higher learning in China, including the University of Nanking, with the Rockefeller Foundation assistance. They together operated in one county in North China as their joint social laboratory and they each contributed their speciality . It was very successful . (1. p. 94). Beginning from 1969, the University of the Philippines College of Agricultur e at Los Banos is operating a social . laboratory in its neighborhood, under the SEARCA (Southeast Asia Regional Center for Graduate Study and Research in Agriculture) program. In 1970 SEARCA is going to advise the Kasetsart University in Thailand in establishing a social laboratory. It is expected that such assistance will be ex- -r:t<..e tended toAother member nations of SEARCA in the near future. Reference 1. Chang, Chi-wen, Rural Asia Marches Forward - Focus on Rural and Agricultural Development, University of the Philippines, College o_f Agriculture, College, ~guna, Philippines, pp. 426.•",
