    "text": "THE UTILIZATION OF EFFECTIVE METHODS IN TEACHING AGRICULTURE AT THE SECONDARY SCHOOL LEVEL - A Cooper ative Project of t he Bureau of Vocational Education and t he U. P. College of Agriculture The t eac hing of agriculture at the secondary school level is both an extensive and expensive endeavor . The 82 national agri cultural high schools, alone , enrolled nearly 30, 000 students dur ing 1966- 67 at a reported cost i n excess of 17 million pesos . Private , municipal , pr ovin- cial, and barrio high school effo r ts , while more diff icult t o assess, are likewise large in magnitude . The preparation of teachers of agricultur e is one of th e primary missions of the eighteen members institutions of the Assoc i ation of Colleges of Agr icultur e LD the Philippi ne s, and of t he several others currently seeki ng membershi p . Fi ve of t hese institutions, those under the j urisdiction of the Bur eau of Vocational Education, reported an enrollme£t of 1, 032 s tudents in t he teacher education curriculum during 1966 -67 .~ . One of t he ma in difficulties of t eachers of a griculture aDd teacher educators a l ike is the dea2th of t extbooks and references appropriate to the Phi lippi ne s etting.~ There is an especially acute need for a book addressed to t he centra l as pe cts of the professional preparation of a t ea che r of agriculture. Such a work s Lould be based on the experience of t he mos t e ffective t eac hers of agriculture and should deal primarily with the us e of various t eac hing meth ods in improving the learning of students in t he agricultu ral schools . I t is to the fulfillment of this task that this pr oject is addressed. PURPOSES 1. To assess the experience of innovative and master teachers in utili- zing various teaching methods to improve the learning of students of vocational agriculture at the secondary school level. 2. To codify this experience into principles and how-to-do-it directions relevant to the professional environment of the teacher of agriculture. 3. To publish and distribute the findings in a textbook appropriate for use in the pre-service preparation of a teacher of agriculture.",
