    "text": "THE DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL EDUCATION .BRIEF HISTORY The Department of Agricultural Education of the UoP. College of Agriculture was established by the Board of Regents of the University of the Philippines i March 1928 by virt~e of Philippine Legislative Act Noo 3377, known as National Vocational Education Act of 1927o This Act authorized, among others, the establishment of a Department of Agricultural Education in the University of the Philippines for the purpose of providing pre~service and in-service training needs for ~eachers, supervisors and administrators of vocationa l agricultural schools in the countryo Formal courses in agricultural education were offered fo r the first time during the second semester of 1929. Together '~ith the department, a University Rural High School was established to serve as a training laboratory for observation and practice teaching and as a n experimental school for secondary education in agriculture. Up to 1938, the main offering of the de partment was a one-year post-B.S.Ao training course leading to the Certificate in Agr ic ultural Education o This course was o pened to colle ge seniors majoring either :tn agronomyp animal husbandry or agric ltural engineering and to those '~ho were already employed as teachers, supe rvisors and administrators of agricultura l sc hools but desire t o get further professional training :L a gr ic ul tura 1 education. In 1938, the first undergraduate thesis or major in agricultural •:ducation wa.:. instit ted. This was the beginning of the agricultural E~duc ation curriculum which was f ormally launched in 1953, with preacribed courses in technical agriculture and professional education. Also i nstituted together with this 4-year BSA agricultural education curriculum",
