    "text": "THE DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATIONS HISTORY Be fore 1954, the College had accumulated volumes of research find i ngs a nd had improved the quality of its instruction o The extension of knowledge in modern farming to the rural areast however, was carried on by differ ent technical departments only to a small degreeo There was a wide gap between agriculture as known by the scientist and agri- culture as practiced by the farmero To help bridge this gap , the Office of Extension and Publications was established in 1954o Staffed by an exchange professor and three information specia lists, the Office produced the Philippine Agriculturistp a monthly technical journal; the Monthly Bulletin, an alumni newspaper; and a few publications and l eaflets o With the creation of the Office, agricul t ural information, which had largely been published in the Philip- pine Agricultur i st, was also made . available through visuals, newspapers, magazines, a bigger volume of publications , as well as through the radio on a limited basis ~ The expansion and growth of personnel, facilities, and services at the College called for the creation of a full-fledged information department. Hence~ in 1962, the Office became the Department of Agri- cultural Information and Communications. FUNC!IONS With its creation, the Department of Agricultural Information research, instruction, and Communications (DAIC) assumed four functions : Thus~ it t eaches courses in agricul- extension , and public informationo",
