    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2030",
    "text": ".. 9 - This evaluation is subjective and should be used with caution. On the other hand if we follow -up those who had undergone the training 2 or 3 years ago we may be able to see whether the training is effective or not depending on what the trained worker s had ac complished. Two - thirds of both combined classes of TA Os and PPis r ated the program excellent and good. This is shown by Figure 4. However, both groups rated it very short with only a diffe rence of 13o/o. Fig 5a. The PPI 's who rated the duration of training very short, rated the daily s e s s ions very tight ( 7lo/o) Figure 5b. Ther e is actually a difference in the length of training in both gl'.911ps. T he TAO group had a 10-day RPTP with morning sessions only (7 a.m. to 2 p.m. ) while the PPI group had a 4 .. day RPTP with whole day sessions, morning and afternoon. VIII. Some Imelications 1. This kind of a training program tends to develop among the participants a deeper understanding and appreciation of the farmer and his problems. 2. That the extension worker would develop enough self-confidence to face with fresh vigor the practical challenges in the field and in fact become a r e cognized leader among farmers and industry representatives. ~ 3. The training of the extension workers alone isAa guarantee that rice yields will increase. The training coupled with a meaningful and realistic program plus appropriate support of the administrators might be the answer.",
