    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2090, part 1",
    "text": "- 4 - cent r of c conut production. However, from t ~1e standpoint of rccrui ting cicntis ts and providing stimulus to their work it would pcr~po be better to fi1m a location near a center of rcse~rch. ' ' Although fishing is an established industry in the ocean, lakes, and ponds, there is a need for modernization. Plans are being made for a research institute for fisheries. Pineapple plantations are being expanded in Mindanao with good prospects for a significant increase in exports. Mindanao also offers a good grazing land for the production of beef. Efforts are being made to establish a dairy industry , and there is every reason to believe that the country can produce dairy products successfully. It is important that precautions be taken that the first herds be kept free of disease and that the first products be sanitary and free of adulteration. The absence of local manufacture of animal feeds also poses a pr obl em in the development of an animal industry. The Dairy Resear ch and Training Institute at Los Ba~s is being set up with technical hel p from FAO . Scientific programs in nutrition and agriculture ar e well organized and the main problems fully recoenized. The National Science and Development Board has established priorities for r esearch and devel opment programs in government and industry. Funds have been allocated t o scientific manpower development and to projects that include a mult ipurpos e pilot plant, a scientific instrumentation center, and a f ood and nutr ition research center . The chairman of the National Science and Devel opment Board is a leading nutritionist. The strong emphas i s on nutrition i n the Philippines began with the famous Bataan exper iment to study t he control of beri-beri by using enriched r ice . The more r ecent I CNND survey has added a further impulse to str engthening the pr ogram of r es earch and education in nutrition . The Food and Nutr ition Research Cent er is establishing f ood composition tabl es and conducting nutrit ion surveys to determine nutr itional status throughout the country. This Cent er is also cooperating with other cent ers in t he National Institute of Science and Technology in the devel",
