    "text": "7 • • 6. ~w.~~~· A world io 1 c nt r for t ining ard res reb in t will provid ub t ntial b nefits to th Colleg ot and to th Philippin s. Food technology is ost clos ~ r ted to th utili2 tion of agricultural products. It contributes to gricultur by providing increased outlets for agricultural pro- duct nd is d perrlent on agriculture for an adequate supply of uita.bl raw materials. Food t ohnology is essential to a well- rounded program 1n a College or .Agriculture if the College is to a si t tb industri s engaged in the processing, storage, distri- bution and merchandizing or roods. In most developing countries more than ba1.f the economy is b ed on agriculture and the proc ssing of agricultural products is ess ntial to the 11Xlustrializat1on or thes countri~. - More sp~ ifi-call_y, food technology can ke the following tw e contr1- buti.ons to the welfare of the Philippines: (1) Increase the availabili't¥ of foreign exchaJ1te bJ' dev loping improved products for export. (2) Increase the tood suppq by the reduction of vaate and the development ot processed tocds thAt are available tbroqbal th year. (') Improve the h lth t>f t",
