    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2269",
    "text": "Tropical Food Processing FS 238 Dbjectives of Course 1. Give instruction in principles and practice of food processing, with emphasis on tropical foods. 2. Survey~ at an advanced level, all techniques available for preserving foods. 3. Show how the basic sciences of chemistry, biochemistry, bacteriology, and engineering dictate practice in food processing operations. Other fields such as econo1nics, packaging, psychology and legal aspects will be touched on. 1- 4. To impart confidence to plan, manage, and operate a complete food processing operation. ecommended Books f or Reading: 1. Blumenthal. 1947 . \" F ood Products\". Chemical Pub. TP 370 B57. 2. von Loesecke . · 1949. 2nd Ed. \"Outlines of .Food Technology\" TP 370 V6 {old; but good) 3. Tressler and Evers. 19 \"Freezing Preservation of F oods 11 • TP 493 T 712 Vol 1 & Vol II. 4. Parker~ Harvey, Stateler. \"Elements of Food Engineering\".. TP 370 P 3 (in 3 volumes) 5. VI . V. Cruess. 3d Ed. \"Comraercial Fruit & Vegetable Products\". TX 601 C 75. 6. J. M. IVIendoza. 1961. \"Philippin e F ocds. . Their Processing and 11 ManufactuX\"e • TP 370 P 55 M 54. 7. I~. B. Jacobs. \"The Cllernistry & Technology of Food & Food Products\". TX 531 ,J 33 (2nd Ed. in 3 volumes) 11 8. S. Y. de Leon . . 11 Preservation of Philippi.ne Foods • TX 601 L 46. 11 9. Borgstrom. ''Fish as Food • (Vols 3 & 4 only} TX 385 B 6 . · 10. American Meat Institute ·Foundation. ;: Science ·of Meat & Meat .. Products\". TX 556 Ni 4 A 5 .",
