    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2270",
    "text": "11. Potter . 1968. \"Food Sci ence'' . 12. Campb ells Book of Canning. 13. F arrall. \"Engineering for Dairy and Food Products\", TP 370 F 3. Chapter 7. \"Steam and its uses in the Dairy\". ppl29-169. INTR.ODUCTION do we eat food? Because we like it . Quality 1) appearance- shape, size, colqr, gloss, surface roughness. 2) flavor- taste (tongue) and odor (nose) . 3) texture - feel in hand, feel in mouth a s chewed. -hardnass, brittleness, chewiness, viscosity, sound. Because we can afford it. VJe buy only those foods that we can afford. Because it is safe. assume free from harmful ingredients and spoilage . For social purposes-most entertainment del:J·ends he avily on food and drink to provide a large measure of the social pleasure. Because it is nutritious . nutrition comes last-very few people eat food because it is good for them, and even if it is nutritious it will not be consumed in quantity unless the eating provides pleasure . 1. Cereals- rice, wheat, corn. 2. lVIeats- pork, beef, lamb, carab~o, goat, rabbit. 3. Fish- lapu-lapu, bangus, lobster, galung.g ong, shelliish, squid. 4. Poultry- chicken, duck, turkey, eggs, pigeons, balut. 5. Vegetables- beans, carrots, cucumbers, cabbage, asparagus, potato. 6. Fruits- banana, pineapple, mango, papaya, chico. 7. Dairy- milk from cow, goat, carabao, cream, ci1eese, butter, ice cre.a m. 8. Fats .. coconut oil, lard, corn oil, margarine, prumoil. (2)",
