    "text": "E. To enable trans portation to a dis tant m arket eg. canned pineapples are sent to Alas ka. Value of Selected F oods Exported by P hilippines 1961 - 1967 in US $ 1, 000 Fresh P r ocessed Value ::12_ Va lue % Fruits & vegs. 4, 958 5.4 86, 930 94.6 Fish 1, 801 82.3 387 17.7 Cereals 187 55 . 5 150 44.5 Me at, poultry eggs 187 97.1 6 2.9 Othe rs 34 0. 7 5, 06 8 99.3 T otal 7, 167 92, 541 F. For Conv enience- saves .time and effor~ in the home. e g. roasting and grinding own coffee beans vs. brewing coffee from ground & roasted beans v s instant coffee vs freeze - dried instant coffee. · G. Econom ic Reasons. eg. Frozen orange concentrate from F lori da sells in; New York cheaper than the equivalent of fresh Florida oranges in New York- reason- saving on contaiaers, shipping cost of water & peel, no wastage. H. Maintain a food stock pile for .e m ergencies . (fire, flood, earthquake, war) Importance of Food Processing In the US 25, 000 technically trained people serve the food industry. It is estimated that 20o/o of food produced in U.S. is lost in wastage, in India 50% is lost. There is great need for more preservation of food in the Philippines to give better quality & less wastage. Perishability of Foods 1. Highly perishable .. last only hours or days before spoiling, receive great attention from food scientist because of pressing need to preserve them. example- fish, meat, milk, many fruits & vegs. (4)",
