    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2404",
    "text": "-· ... ,- 24 disintegration of the bean structure . Cooking could still be further increased with a steam process . However , these beans were acceptable to the infants. Coconut Milk Beverages Coconut milk was prepared b y shredd i ng the fresh coconut meat and pressing it with added wa ter in the proportion of 1:1 (W/V) . The coconut milk was filtere d through a cloth filte r. It was bottled in 8- ounce so f t d rink bottles with and without 5 % adde d sucrose and sterili zed in the bottle for 10 minute s a t 250° F . It was found t h at the coconut protein c o a g ula t ed when h eated, somewhat like di l u te milk-egg custard . Al t h ough coagulation occurred , u po n shaking, the curd tende d t o r e disperse into a milk. I The flavo r of the coconut milk containing 5 % sucrose was excellent, sweet , and d efinitely coconut in characte r. Mixed with soybean I milk 1:9 (V/ V), it imparted a ple a sant coconut flavor to the resulting milk. As little as 1 part coconut milk to 19 parts soy- I bean milk introduced a pleas a nt coconut flavor masking the usual I soybean flavor. In higher concentrations, the coconut milk could be used as I pudding. I Coconut Protein Stud ie s Fermentation as a method of separating coconut oil and protein I was investigated . various patented a n d published methods of extracting oil from",
