    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2514",
    "text": "- 4 - skills, humanities, social sciences, and modern languages~ With the institution of Western Thought II last school year, 1966-67, the total course offerings of the Department reached 21, all 3-unit courses, as follows: English I* English II* English 10 Humanities I* English III* Speech I* Asian Civilizations* Philippine Histroy & Institutions I* Western Thought I* Western Thought II* Philippine Institutions 100 Spanish I* Spanish II* Spanish 12* Spanish 13* French la French lb German la German lb German 2a German 2b Of the 21 courses, 13 (marked with asterisks above) are general education courses. Equivalent to 39 credit units, these courses constitute about 80 percent of the general education course offerings for the different undergraduate curricula of the Collegeo Though it serves the College of Agriculture mainly, the Department also serves the College of Forestry partly by way of its general education course offerings. For this purpose, the Department of Humanities, more than any other department in the College, carries the greatest bulk of the instructional program which underlies University education in agriculture and other professionso",
