    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2515",
    "text": "- 5 - The Dep rtmentvs participation in the College gradua te progr am has so far been limited to giving examinations for r eading knowledge i n for e i gn languages, aside from its language course offerings that pr epar e students fo r these examinationso However, there has been greater use of these language course offerings by gr aduate students t o ful f i ll the i r foreign language requirementso Whereas German and French used to be the only I languages in demand~ even Spanish and English have i n recent years I become useful to gr a duate s t udents 9 particularly scholars from the I Interna tional Rice Re s earch Ins t ituteo Unlike most depar t ment s i n t he College 9 the Department of I Humanitie s does not offer degree courseso I Re sear ch and cr eative worko The research and creative work of I the Depart ment fa lls into t wo categories ~ (1) the main contributions I to schol ar ship o f a staff member as he works to fulfill the requirements I for a particular degree, and (2) ot her activities of the faculty, I largely extracurricul ar, which help keep ali ve the spirit of creative \\ researcho I I n the f i rs t ca t egory, the contributions of the Department are I the finished or current graduate theses of its staff memberso I The research and creative output in the second category reflects b the Department and the I dl d the rich variety of subject areas han e Y l versatil ity of the staff. Among the activities of the staff in this j direction are the following: and semi-monthly department lo Delivering c ol lege c olloquiums hilosophy, the arts, political P seminars in which problems of literature p thought , and teaching methods are discussedo",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
