    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2516",
    "text": "- 6 - Conducting workshops on creative writing, play productions and the fine rtso Writing short stories, poems, plays, feature articles and essays for local and national magazineso 4o Performing in the arts including landscape design, the drama, ballet and folk dance, paintingo In this activity area, the Depa~tment points with pride to its Shakespeare Festival and to other productions in which the staff were fully engaged as actors, directors, or as members of the production staff. In its research and creative activities, the Department seeks to complement the heavily technical training offered by the Collegeo Properly, the role of the Department in this community complex is to promote knowledge of and appreciation for the humanities, without which it cannot be truly said that a student 9 s education is well-rounded. Extension and community service. Because of the nature of its subject areas, the Department has a unique function in the College Extension Program. Instead of dealing directly with the farmers and their families, the end-users of technological information disseminated through the extension program, the Department seeks to promote the development of those skills which will facilitate the extension of agricultural knowledge. The role of the Department, therefore, in the college Extension Program lies in extension education. The Department helps in the training of extension personnel not only of the College but also of other agencies, especially in developing such important skills as oral and written communication. To this end, the Department has",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
