    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2521",
    "text": "DEPARTMENT OF PlANT PATHOLOGY Historical Background The founding of t he U. P. College of Agriculture, at Los Bafios in 1909» afforded an institution ~7hich led in the basic and applied studies of plant diseaseso No less than the first dean of the C ollege, Dr. E. B• • Copeland who realized the importance of plant diseases, was instrumental in organizing the department. Since its founding in 1917, the department has been proud of its men who have led it. Dr. c. F. Baker (1912) began the extensive collec- tion of Philippine fungi; Dr. Otto Reinking (1916) offered the first course in plant pathology and published a brief study of diseases of economic plants in the Philippines ; Dr. Gerardo G. Ocfemia (1918-1959), the father of plant pathology in the Philippines, was well known for his works on the diseases caused by viruses. Dr. F. T. Orillo (1955-1960), the present Director of Research of the College and Professor Victoria M. E1a, the present chairman of the department~ have been responsible in organizing the graduate program of the department. The department, in keeping pace with the development program of the college and the food production campaign of the nation, fulfills its functions and responsibilities through instruction, research, and exten- sion . Research The department offers various areas of specialization in the field of plant pathology. Major students can choose the field of specialization that suits their interest and capabilities. These areas of specialization are~",
