    "text": "CORNELL UNIVERSITY NE\\\\7 YORK STATE AGRICULTIJRAL EXPERIMENT STATION GENEVA, NEW YORK 14456 A DIVISION OF TUE NE\\V YORK STATE COLLEGE OF AGRICULTURE, ITIIACA, NE W YORK A STATUTORY COLLEGE OF Till:: STATE UNIVERSITY CHARLBS B. PALM, Dllo\\N OP 'l'Hll COLLIIGB DONALD w. BARTON, DIRBC'l'OI\\ Ol' 'l'HB STATION OFFICE OF THE DIRECTOR March LJ. , 1968 MEMORANDUM RECE:!VED TO: Dean and Directors Provost D. R. Corson M.4R F) - I~OJ Vice-Provost W. K. Kennedy D::,~N's OFFICe ~\">-~~~~' - N FROM : D. W. Barton · Y. S. Coda0 0 cf A . \"\" 9rtculture SUBJECT: Report on an Administrative Review o f the University of the Philippines - Cornell Unive rs ity Gr aduate Education Program I am enclosing a c opy of the nReport on an Administrative Review of the UP - Cornell Graduate Education Pro gram, January 20 ·- February 16, 1968n . This report was prepar ed f or limited distri - bution, and puts forth observations made by me to Dean Umali , based on my review conducted du r i ng a fo ur-week period . Since my assignment was not in the na ture of a consultant , and the contents of the report deal primarily wi th admi nistrative matters, this has not been released f or gene ral distribution. Copies were sent to Dean Umali for the us e of his administrative staff . Additionally, the details in the r eport were covered in specific oral sessions with the Dean and Di rectors at UPCA . I , personally , found the r eview a very educational experience . I am impressed with the rapidl y increasing quality of staff at Los Banos . The opp ortunitie s f or strengthening the College program are great . Additi onally, it is my impression that the quality of leadership b eing provi ded by Cornell through the project leader and through Cornell consultants, is excellent . I hope t hat you will f ind this report of value in our c ontinuing effort with the University of the Philippines .",
