    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2622",
    "text": "- 5 - was t h e r e c e nt s taffing study in the Crop Protection Depa rtments , Pla nt Patholo gy a nd Entomology. Thi s Report was prepared by a Committe e compris e d of m e mbers from several departments in a ddition to the two mentioned above.. The Department of Agronomy also provided a copy of its \"First Research Review\". This kind of documenta tion and self analysis is valuable, not only to departmental staff, but also the administrative staff who must do salesmanship of the College research effort .. Acreages, production, and peso values are given for major agricultural c ommodities or commodity groups for the Philippines , and outstanding problems are listed, with the departmental effort d efined . '-, During the depa r tmental r e vi ews , it was encouraging to note that some departments are listing \"unde rgraduate research\" separately from departmental research programs. This is quite appropriate. With competent research professors, significant contributions from their research should be expected . Their projects comprise the mainstream of departmental research effort. Co-listing of under- graduate theses creates a confusion to the outsider about where the major departmental effort is being placed. One department is con- solidating major projects into program areas. This may be useful in avoiding a tendency to equate res~arch productivity with the projects listed for a professor.",
