    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2623",
    "text": "t th i nt• a ar o'n t 0 c ar e number of agricultur p ob em o a ne ds o be done . There is a general awareness of i ation, and a hope expressed that as staff that are away in aining return, the research load can be better distributed. ollowing the departmental reviews, conferences were held individually with the Director of Research, Director of Graduate Education, and Director {and past Director} of Business Affairs. Thes conferences were very useful in clearing up some specific questions about personnel and research administration, and the budget and budgeting process . These conferences also afforded an opportunity to brief the Directors on newer aspects of r esea rch administration and coordination within the United States. Opportunity was taken to discuss many of the elements of this report. It should be stated at this point that the primary administrative goals set forth in the later stages of this report offer no new ideas. The Directors are very well informed about these matters, and quite competent to move ahead in College planning. The Annual Report was very useful in the review of the College of Agriculture . The \"highlight\" section makes it easy for one to grasp the scope and accomplishments of the College, without a detailed study of the total report. It was stated in the Publications Department that",
