    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2909",
    "text": "NEW YO K STATE COLLEGE OF AGR ICULTURE 400 ROBERTS HALL UNIVERSITY I TEL. ITHACA, NEW YORK AR 5-3158 For Immediate Use Ithaca, N . Y .~ May - Dean D. L . Umali of t he College of Agri- culture and vice president fo r Agri cultural and Forestry Affairs, University of the Philippines , arrived here Monday for discu ssions with officials of the N.Y. St ate College of Agriculture, . Cornell University. He will confer wlth Dean Charles E. Palm of the College of . Agriculture , and Prof. Kenne th L. Turk, director of international agricultural development for the college, on a new proposed cooperative agreement betwe en their colleges. The two institutions had a contract arrangement from 1952 to 1960 under which Cornell pr ofessors were assigned to the University of the Philippines and young Filipino staff members came to Cornell for graduate t raining . Dean Umali, who earned the Ph.D. degree at Cornell in 1949, i s making his first return trip t o t he campus. He is accompanied by Mrs. Umali . The Philippine agricultural and educational leader also will meet with directors of research, instruction, and extension at the College of Agriculture . He will confer with other university officials and various department heads. As official Philippine representative to the World Food Con- gress, Dean Umali will be in Washington, D.C., from June 3 to 18. While there, he will confer with officials of the Agency for Inter- national Development, the World Bank, and the U.S. Dept. of ,· 225-40 52763 (more) Cooperative Extension Service, New York State Colleges of Agriculture and Home E • t De partmen t of Agricultu re cooperating . In furtherance of Acts of Congress May 8 J~~:o;~csl ;l ~ornAell University a~d the United St~tes • , ~. . A. Johnson, D1rector of Extens1on.",
