    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2910",
    "text": "page 2 - Dean Umali Agriculture . He will return to Cornell on June 19 for further consultations wi th s taff members in the College of Agriculture • . Later he wi ll consult with officials of the Ford and Rocke- feller Founda t i ons, and the Council of Economic and Cultural Affairs in New York City. He and Mrs. Umali also will visit North Carolina State College J the University of Minnesota, the University of Calif ornia, the East-West Center in Honolulu, and the University of Hawaii. Dean Umali~ who was graduated from the University of the Philippines College of Agriculture at Los Banos in 1939, has headed several agricultural~ educational, research, and civic organizations, and today is chairman, director, or member of many groups. In 1949~ he started the breeding and selection of superior rice varieties and the development of hybrid corn adapted to the Philippines. As a result of his efforts and those or his associ- ates, the rice and corn seed improvement program has produced 14 outstanding rice varieties and five corn hybrids approved and recommended by the Philippine Seed Board. He was presented the \"Award of Merit for Outstanding Achieve- ment and Leadership in Ric e and Corn Research\" by Philippine President Carlos P. Garcia in 1958. He is the holder of several citations~ is a member of many professional organizations in the United States and the Philippines, has held seveaal research and professorial positions, and has participated in seed improvement and plant breeding conferences in many parts of the world. -30-",
