    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2918",
    "text": "NEW YORK STATE COLLEGE OF AGRICULTURE A UNIT OF THE STATE UNIVERSITY OF NEW YORK CORNELL UNIVERSITY ITHACA, NEW YORK CHARLES E . AL DEA. June 24, 1963 To Members of the Faculty of the College of Agricul ture: Dean D. J. Umali from the College of Agriculture, University of the Philippines at Los Banos, will address our faculty on Friday morning, June 28, at 11 o'clock in Room 45 Warren Hall. As mos t of you know, Dean Umali is also the Vice-President for Agricultural and Forestry Affairs of the University of the Philippines. He and Mrs. Umali have been in the United States since early June spending time with us and in attendance at the World Food Congress. Shortly he will be leaving for home via the Universities of Minnesota, California and Hawaii. Dean Umali is a Corne llian, having received his PhD. in Plant Breeding in 1949. His outstanding contributions to the agriculture of the Philippines, and to southeast Asia, are well known. We look forward with much pleasure to the future relationships between Los Banos and Cornell. If your schedule permits, I am confident that you will enjoy hearing Dean Umali, learning more about the program for building his colleges at Los Banos, and asking him questions which may arise from his presentation. (j~!}~ Charles E. Palm Dean CEP:am",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
