    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2925, part 2",
    "text": "ry of Agriculture Orville L. Freeman, \"by one of the most fortunate coincidences of history .-• He points out that when more than half of humanity does not have enough to eat , and livesin poverty and misery, the developed nations are producing an abundance of food, through the application of science and technology.",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
