    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2927, part 2",
    "text": "Banos to carry on the work and the fine tradition of t he college. I n the tremendous task of starting all over a~ain we received mu ch support from the u. s. government (AID~, the Rockef el ler Foundation, CECA, and our National Govern- ment . Notabl e among the many forms of aid given us by the American Government was the Cornell-Los Banos Contract \"to assist in the rehabilitation of the College of Agri- culture , the development of the Central Experiment Station, the training of pr ofessional agricultural personnel in research, t eachi ng and extension, and the development of educational materi a l s .\" The success of this contract was largely due to t he personnel assigned to the program, the program i t se lf, and the area in which it operated.",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
