    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2928, part 1",
    "text": "-4- The visiting professors were the most direct f aetor rom the U S side that influenced the course and op - eration of the program . Our College was consu l ted bef ore these professors were sent and Cornell Uni vers i t y sent the leading educators and scientists a vai l able . They easily won from us the respect t ha t is so e ssentia l to productive work . They possessed many impor tant quali- ties so necessary in technical ass i s t a nce programB . Adaptable to cultural diff erences , they had other traits , such as sympathy and tact , i ngenui t y, and pers everance and good health, that made them opera te effectively i n a different environment . The Cornellians worked with us in the f iel ds , under the sun and rain , in the mud , although it wou ld ha ve been easy for them to enj oy the cool comfort of a ir-conditioned rooms and to be among the cocktail group of Americans in the city . And when anything was achie ved, they did not try to take or cl a im the credit sol e ly for themselves··· They never a cted or pretended to be a dvis ors or super- visors . They t rea ted their Fil i pi no counterparts as their equal s . They built up their counterpa rts, not themselves . They lived in our community. Their children attended the same schools as ours and associated with our children . These professors • children learned to speak our nat i onal language (Tagalog ) s o well that, unless we could see t hem, it became incr easingly difficult to tell them apart from our own . For the qualities of the long-range College program t hat were i mplemented , some of the more important are the f ollowing. The programs pr ovided for a smooth continuity of plans and projects . Generally, a visiting professor served a tou r of dut y of one to one and a half years. If by then a project had not been completed, arrangements were made so that the new man could continue it. It was significant that a specific period of service v-1as set f'or each vis iting professor assigned in Los Banos. He was expected, i f poss ible, to accomplish his goals within t his time . Ext ension of a visiting professor's stay, however , could be made if needed. Activities under the program were",
