    "title": "Cornell (1).txt: OCR page 2928, part 2",
    "text": "expected, i f poss ible, to accomplish his goals within t his time . Ext ension of a visiting professor's stay, however , could be made if needed. Activities under the program were geared to Phil·i ppine condit i ons and needs of the country for its over-all socio- economic development. The two groups con- sult ed wi th each other before undertaking any project. They dec i ded what and how projects would be carried out with no other cr iterion but the merits of the projects. The Cornell prof ess ors built on the resources available in the Col lege . They did not make replicas of the costly American laborator i es they had been used to.",
    "href": "Cornell (1).txt"
